This file is stamped automatically when the project is downloaded from GitHub
as a ZIP or tarball. If the lines above still read "$Format:...$", you are in a
git working checkout rather than an extracted archive — ask git instead:

    git describe --tags --always

The extracted FOLDER carries the version only when you download from a tag or
release (Longbarrow-1.12.0/). A download from a branch is named after the
branch (Longbarrow-main/), because that is how GitHub names archives and it is
not something the repository can override. Use the Releases page, or the tag
you want, to get a version-stamped folder.
